<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seraing</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seraing is an industrial town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> just upstream of Liège, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>. In 1817 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-cockerill">John Cockerill</a> set up ironworks and engineering shops in the former summer palace of the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> there, and the Cockerill works became one of the largest industrial enterprises of continental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seraing.jpg" alt="Seraing" width="320" height="255" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: flamenc · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seraing_-_Casa_de_la_vila.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
